{
  "story": "§6.4: the erasure of the account a subscription is bound to unbinds it at the erasure, recording `unbound` under that account, and leaves every period the account held with no one: no later event of one names an account, and an account that claims the subscription (R-9) is not told them again (INV-13). A period paid after the erasure follows the binding, so the claimant holds Windmill One at once and the period it paid for is recorded under it. An erasure repeated changes nothing.",
